1. She is a celestial messenger who got hit by a truck and was isekai’d into becoming British. (Verbatim: "I'm a celestial messenger that got hit by a truck and got isekhied and became British. That is my lore.")  
2. Her full name is Elia Stellaria. (Verbatim: "I'm Elias Alaria, British VTuber") [Note: likely phonetic/spoken variation of "Elia Stellaria"]  
3. She is scared of butterflies and flying creatures, possibly due to bright accessories attracting them. (Verbatim: "I'm normally scared of butterflies and any flying things... I think it might be the big bow, but yes.")  
4. She has wings but is too afraid to use them and does not have a flying license. (Verbatim: "I do have wings, technically. Which I hear, but I'm too scared to use them.")  
5. Her birthday is on March 7th. (Verbatim: "It's not my birthday. It's not until the 7th of March, okay?")  
6. She dislikes flying and finds it frightening despite having wings. (Verbatim: "I'm also very scared of flying.")  
7. She wants to make her audience smile and sees that as her current purpose. (Verbatim: "right now my meaning is to try and make you all smile.")  
8. She has a fondness for rose arches and wants one in her own garden someday, inspired by her parents’ garden. (Verbatim: "We had this rose arch in the garden... if I was to ever get my own place and a garden, I would want to get a rose arch.")  
9. She loves roses and associates them with her parents’ home. (Verbatim: "I really like roses. The place, like my parents' place. We had this rose arch in the garden.")  
10. She plans to buy discounted British chocolate after Valentine’s Day, indicating a habit or interest in post-holiday deals. (Verbatim: "we'll enjoy the Valentine's Day at Onsen with you! ... I'm very excited to go to the shop and get all the discounted British chocolate.") [end of text]



1. She attended a Catholic school and was required to attend Roman Catholic Church every Sunday. (Verbatim: "I had to go to a catholic school and I was made to go to the roman catholic church every sunday")
2. She no longer attends church since becoming an adult, which upset her family. (Verbatim: "As soon as I became an adult they were like you can choose and I was like okay bye they were so mad")
3. She worked in an office environment where employees took turns hosting weekly quizzes. (Verbatim: "This was when I was working at the office and we had to do every wednesday each employee would have take a turn in doing a quiz")
4. She has a strong interest in McDonald's, having created multiple themed quizzes about its global locations and menu items. (Verbatim: "When it was my turn I did a quiz on mcdonald's... next time I did another one on mcdonald's food items and which country they're sold in")
5. She is from England, where pub culture and pub quizzes are common. (Verbatim: "Drinking culture is very big in england... they'd have like these like student places")
6. She is uncomfortable in loud, crowded bars and prefers cozy, quiet environments. (Verbatim: "I remember the first time I walked into an english pub and I died inside... I much prefer somewhere comfy cozy and cute like here")
7. She finds general knowledge, music, and sports topics difficult, especially in quiz settings. (Verbatim: "In terms of general I have no knowledge in the general department so I struggle... music again not my forte and sports not my forte")
8. She once helped a team during a pub quiz because of her knowledge of the Bible, gained from Catholic school. (Verbatim: "It was only because for some reason one question... was related to the bible and I was like I know this I went to catholic school")
9. She is uncomfortable with sports bars and associates them with intimidating stereotypes. (Verbatim: "Those also scare me so I don't know what to picture at a sports bar I just picture a bunch of sports people being like er sports lads lads lads")
10. She used to drink alcohol, indicating she is of legal drinking age. (Verbatim: "Oh, then you are of legal age") [end of text]



1. She used to attend the Roman Catholic Church regularly but stopped going after becoming an adult. (Verbatim: "the roman catholic church every sunday um can't confirm i don't have to go anymore as soon as i became an adult they were like you can choose and i was like okay bye")

2. She believes in being kind, respectful, and empathetic as her personal moral code, independent of organized religion. (Verbatim: "i just like the idea of being kind and being respectful and being empathetic like all the other stuff i don't know")

3. She is required to attend church during Christmas and sometimes Easter when she is at home with her family. (Verbatim: "i have to go at christmas so yeah christmas time i have to go um and if i'm at home around easter time then probably around easter")

4. She visited an onsen town called Kinosaki in Japan and highly recommends it, especially for foreigners with tattoos. (Verbatim: "i went to an onsen town called kinosaki i highly recommend kinosaki it's also very welcoming to foreigners especially if you're worried about if you have any tattoos")

5. She finds some onsen baths too hot to stay in for long, recalling one that left her bright red. (Verbatim: "one of them was was was one i couldn't really spend a long time in because it was way too hot it was way too way too way too hot i went in and by when i got out i was bright red")

6. She enjoys hopping between hot and cold baths, especially during summertime. (Verbatim: "what i like to do is hop between the hot and the cold baths")

7. She had a memorable experience eating ice cream after an onsen bath in Japan, which she found especially delicious. (Verbatim: "i had ice cream i had ice cream i remember i got out the onsen put on my yukata walked over and was like yeah like yeah ice cream ice cream and it felt it tasted so good")

8. She stayed in a fancy onsen room that had its own private pool. (Verbatim: "we got the fanciest room in the onsen see we have our own pool in the middle")

9. She has a notably long neck, which she jokes about but clarifies she is not a goose. (Verbatim: "i do have a long neck it's not because i'm a goose though um i was just born with it")

10. The onsen setting in the stream is fictional, located in the "celestial realm" and copied from Earth, indicating a fantasy backdrop for her persona. (Verbatim: "well this onsen is in the celestial realm that got copied from earth so i don't know about the time of year or anything because nothing makes sense") [end of text]



1. She is British. (Verbatim: "i'm just british um")  
2. She struggles with expressing emotions in words, especially due to her upbringing. (Verbatim: "words really aren't my forte um especially since i grew up in a household that does not talk about feelings in the slightest ever")  
3. She has a habit of repeating phrases like "I'll work hard" because she doesn't know what else to say. (Verbatim: "i tend to just make noises and stuff and i tend to repeat a lot of the same phrases of you know i'll work hard i'll do my bestest and that kind of thing because i don't know what to say")  
4. She experiences constant self-doubt and a fear of not being enough as a VTuber. (Verbatim: "i always feel like i'm not doing enough i need to work hard and i need to keep working hard")  
5. She wants to make people happy and believes that is the purpose of being a VTuber. (Verbatim: "we're vtubers to make people happy and that's that's what i want to try and do")  
6. She finds time zones difficult and is often affected by them. (Verbatim: "time zones are my enemy they are like yo oh gosh oh gosh oh gosh yeah")  
7. She enjoys games like Final Fantasy 14 that allow her to escape and immerse herself. (Verbatim: "I think that's why I love games like Final Fantasy 14 and stuff ones where you can really just dive in and and escape")  
8. She is working on improving her roleplay skills. (Verbatim: "I'm still not very good at this whole role play thing but I'm working on it")  
9. She feels deeply motivated and supported by her audience despite her insecurities. (Verbatim: "you guys always manage to make me feel special so thank you for doing that")  
10. She associates warmth and comfort with positive experiences, such as hoping the stream felt like "a warm hot chocolate on a cold day." (Verbatim: "i hope today tastes like um what tastes like feels like a warm warm hot chocolate on a cold cold day") [end of text]



